  provenance: "Sources and tags in full: Assets/Air Wing/Calibration~/F18E-SOURCES.md
    (read 2026-10-25).\nPUBLIC = official page; CALIBRATED = fitted to one public
    figure (C16); AUTHORED = our estimate.\n\nspanFt 44.9: PUBLIC, Navy fact file
    (Wingspan 44.9 ft); Boeing agrees.\nengineCount 2: PUBLIC, Navy fact file (two
    F414-GE-400).\nmaxThrustPerEngineLbf 22000: PUBLIC, Navy fact file and GE F414
    datasheet (22,000 lb static). Conflict: Boeing says 17,000 lb per engine.\nmilitaryThrustPerEngineLbf
    13000: AUTHORED (commonly quoted dry thrust; not on Navy, Boeing or GE pages).\nwingAreaFt2
    500: AUTHORED (secondary sources agree; no official page found).\nemptyWeightLb
    32081: AUTHORED (secondary sources 30,600 to 32,100 lb).\ninternalFuelLb 14400:
    AUTHORED (secondary sources 14,400 to 14,700 lb).\ncd0 0.025: AUTHORED (textbook
    fighter with pylons; NASA Hornet data at L1).\noswaldEfficiency 0.80: AUTHORED
    (textbook).\nclMax 1.6: AUTHORED (clean).\nclMaxNegative 0.8: AUTHORED (half
    of clMax).\nclAlphaPerRad 3.5: AUTHORED (low aspect ratio; sets the HUD's angle
    of attack only).\nflapsDeltaClMax 0.5, flapsDeltaCd 0.04: AUTHORED.\nspeedBrakeDeltaCd
    0.05: AUTHORED (no dedicated speed brake; control surfaces do it).\nidleThrustFraction
    0.05: AUTHORED.\nthrustLapseExponent 1.2726: CALIBRATED to the service ceiling
    50,000 ft (Navy fact file and Boeing, 50,000+ ft) at empty + half internal fuel,
    clean, maximum afterburner, climb speeds up to Mach 0.9 (Calibration~/l0_calibration.py).\nloadFactorMax
    7.5, loadFactorMin -3.0: AUTHORED (widely quoted; not on the official pages found).\nrollRateMaxDegS
    150: AUTHORED.\nloadFactorTimeConstantS 0.25, rollTimeConstantS 0.30: AUTHORED
    (L0 control-law response).\nVALIDATION, not fitted: maximum speed Mach 1.8+ (Navy)
    / Mach 1.6 (Boeing); L0 gives Mach 1.41 at 40,000 ft and 1.54 at sea level (no
    Mach effects until L2).\n\n--- Airframe L1 (W32) ---\ncma, cmds, cmq, cLift,
    cLiftDs, cDrag, cDrag0, cDragDs, cyb, cyda, cydr, clb, clda, cldr, clp, clr,
    cnb, cnda, cndr, cnp, cnr: PUBLIC (W32): the F/A-18 HARV polynomial fits of Chakraborty,
    Seiler and Balas, J. Guidance 34(1) 2011, Appendix Tables A1-A2, fitted to NASA
    HARV flight data; checked against the authors' F18AeroData.mat. Valid for alpha
    0-60 deg; alphaMinDeg -10 and alphaMaxDeg 60: AUTHORED, the polynomials held
    flat outside them. Sideslip enters linearly; no flaps or speed brake in the fits
    (the L0 increments are used, AUTHORED). Applied to the E's own wing (500 ft2,
    44.9 ft): the E is flown on the A/B's coefficients, scaled by its reference geometry
    (AUTHORED, W8).\nmeanChordFt 12.0: AUTHORED, the HARV's 11.52 ft times (S_E/S_A)/(b_E/b_A).\nixxSlugFt2,
    iyySlugFt2, izzSlugFt2, ixzSlugFt2: AUTHORED, NASA TM-107601 Table 3.5 (33,310
    lb: Ixx 23,000, Iyy 151,293, Izz 169,945, Ixz -2,971 slug ft2) scaled as m r2
    to the E at 60 % fuel (40721 lb, mass x1.2225); roll by span (44.9/37.42 ft),
    pitch and yaw by length (60.3/56 ft, Navy fact files), the product by both: Ixx
    40482, Iyy 214448, Izz 240886, Ixz -4693 slug ft2. Fixed at L1; fuel burn moves
    them at L3.\ndragFloorCd0, dragFloorK: AUTHORED, the L0 polar (cd0 and 1/(pi
    e AR)) as a floor under the fits' drag, which is almost nil at low alpha (C_D
    0.004 at alpha 0; the authors note their low-alpha data are thin).\nspoolUpTauS
    1.2, spoolDownTauS 0.8, afterburnerLightTauS 0.4, afterburnerOffTauS 0.25, afterburnerMinSpool
    0.9: AUTHORED, Powerplant L1's spool (slice 2c); no public F414 spool figures
    were found.\nFlight Controls L1 (slice 2b, W23): alphaLimitDeg 30, loadFactorCommandTauS
    0.3, alphaGainPerS 2, loadFactorIntegralDegPerGs 1.15, pitchRateBandwidth 6,
    rollRateBandwidth 5, yawRateBandwidth 3, sideslipGainPerS 2, sideslipPerPedalDeg
    8: AUTHORED, a nonlinear-dynamic-inversion law after Snell, Enns and Garrard
    (J. Guidance 15(4), 1992), tuned in Calibration~/l1_fbw_mirror.py against criteria
    fixed before tuning (ROADMAP slice 2b). stabilatorBandwidth, stabilatorRateDegS,
    stabilatorMinDeg, stabilatorMaxDeg, aileronBandwidth, aileronRateDegS, aileronMinDeg,
    aileronMaxDeg, rudderBandwidth, rudderRateDegS, rudderMinDeg, rudderMaxDeg: PUBLIC,
    the actuators of NASA TM-107601 as Chakraborty, Seiler and Balas 2011 Table 2
    gives them (30, 48, 40 rad/s lags; 40, 100, 61 deg/s; -24..10.5, -25..45, -30..30
    deg).\nLanding Gear L1 (slice 2d, W4): wheels (nose 0,-1.71,5.17; mains +-1.40,-1.71,-0.74
    m about the centre of mass), travelM 0.3, springNPerM 188e3 nose and 661e3 mains,
    damperNsPerM 25e3 and 88e3 (about half critical), hardPointsM (belly, tail, nose,
    wingtips): AUTHORED, measured off the F-18E model with its centre of mass 1.6
    m aft of the model's origin; the springs sized so the static weight compresses
    each strut about half its travel. gearMaxSinkRateFtS 24: AUTHORED, the carrier-landing
    design sink rate commonly quoted for Navy jets (source not pinned), used here
    for any landing. tyreRollingFriction 0.02, tyreBrakingFriction 0.5, tyreLateralFriction
    0.7, tyreSlipSpeedMps 0.5: AUTHORED, textbook dry-concrete tyre values. nosewheelSteerMaxDeg
    20, nosewheelSteerFadeStartKt 40, nosewheelSteerFadeEndKt 80, gearTransitTimeS
    4, gearDownDeltaCd 0.02: AUTHORED. strutEndStopFraction 0.7, strutEndStopStiffening
    30: AUTHORED (SIX, 2026-10-26), an oleo's stiffening air spring near full stroke,
    sized so a hands-off touchdown's nose slap does not bottom the nose strut.\nNote:
    the published f18full.m adds the thrust term of beta-dot with the wrong sign
    (T cos(alpha) sin(beta)/(mV)); Air Wing derives its motion from body kinematics
    and does not inherit it (Calibration~/l1_harv_mirror.py).\n\n--- Gun and combat
    (Gunnery K4, K5) ---\ngunName M61A2 20 mm; gunRoundsPerMinute 6000 and gunRoundsCarried
    412: PUBLIC, General Dynamics OTS, F/A-18 E/F 20 mm gun system sheet (4,000 or
    6,000 shots a minute; the high rate used). gunMuzzleVelocityFtS 3450: SECONDARY,
    a simulator reference's figure for PGU-28/B (not pinned for the E/F's gun). gunRoundMassKg
    0.1, gunRoundDiameterM 0.02, gunRoundFormFactor 1.0 (on G7), gunDispersionMils
    4, gunMaxTimeOfFlightS 3: AUTHORED. gunMuzzleM (0, 0.5, 7.5) and gunBoreBody
    1 deg up: AUTHORED off the model. hitPoints 10 and hitRadiusM 4: AUTHORED, abstract
    (Gunnery K5): a hit is one round, ten shoot the jet down.\n\n--- Game missiles
    (W65) ---\nmissileName 'SR-IR game missile': a generic short-range heat-seeker
    archetype for a video game (SIX 2026-10-29, Air Wing W65); not any real missile,
    no real data. All AUTHORED: four pylons, two under each wing at (\xB14.2, \u22120.45,
    \u22121.8) and (\xB12.6, \u22120.55, \u22121.2) m, off the model; missileBoostAccelMps2
    100 for missileBurnS 3 (about 2.5 times a 400 kt jet), missileDragPerM 3e-5 (k\xB7v\xB2;
    a tail chase from 3 km closes inside the life, one from 5 km on a jet running
    away does not), missileMaxG 30, missileNavGain 4 (proportional navigation, textbook
    3\u20135), missileSeekerConeDeg 45; the lock (SIX's picks): missileLockConeDeg
    30, missileLockMinM 500, missileLockMaxM 5000, missileLockTimeS 1; missileArmS
    0.5, missileLifeS 20; the hit (SIX's picks): missileLethalRadiusM 15, missileKillChance
    0.7, missileDamageHp 6; missileLaunchIntervalS 1.\n\n--- Radar and signature
    (SENSORS-CONCEPT J1) ---\nradarName 'Generic fighter radar (game)': a generic
    nose radar for a video game (SIX 2026-10-29, SENSORS-CONCEPT J1); not any real
    radar, no real data. All AUTHORED: radarGainDbi 33, radarFrequencyHz 10e9 (X
    band), radarBandwidthHz 1e6, radarNoiseFigureDb 4, radarLossesDb 8, radarPulsesIntegrated
    32, radarClutterImprovementDb 30, beamwidths 3.3\xB0, monopulse slope 1.6, floors
    15 m and 0.1\xB0, false alarms 1e-6. radarPeakPowerW 16856 is SOLVED: a 5 dBsm
    target at 40 km is seen on half the search looks (Swerling 1). Modes (J6, body
    frame): range-while-search \xB160\xB0 by \u221230\u2026+30\xB0, 40 km, 4 s frame;
    track-while-scan \xB130\xB0 by \u221220\u2026+20\xB0, 40 km, 2 s; dogfight \xB110\xB0
    by \u221210\u2026+50\xB0, 10 km, 0.5 s. Single-target track (J2), all AUTHORED:
    radarGimbalHalfDeg 60, radarSttRangeM 40000, radarSttLookS 0.1 (ten looks a second),
    radarSttGainDb 6, radarSttDropMisses 10 (a second of misses loses the lock).
    Track file, all AUTHORED: radarTrackSigmaM 150, radarTrackMaxSpeedMps 700, radarTrackMaxAccelMps2
    90 (a 9 G turn), radarConfirmHits 2 of radarConfirmLooks 3 to confirm, radarDropAfterMisses
    3. Starts in range-while-search. Signature: rcsNoseDbsm 3, rcsBeamDbsm 12, rcsTailDbsm
    7 (a generic fighter)."
